	affiliations = {40, rue Camot, Le Crotoy, F-80550, France; Groupe Omithologique Picard, le Bout des Crocs, Saint-Quentin-en-Tourmont, F-80120, France},
	abstract = {The Somme estuary is both an important wintering area for Oystercatchers and one of France's main sites for commercial cockle fishing. The latter is subject to inter-annual variations due to the random recruitment of cockles, which also leads to variations in the diet of Oystercatchers within the same year and from one year to the next. Individual biomass consumption by oystercatchers varies from 271 grams (wet weight with shell) in October to 377 grams in January, depending on température changes. Total consumption by oystercatchers is around 675 tonnes of cockles, all size classes combined, per winter. This consumption accounts for 22 ± 17% of cockle mortality, while commercial fishing accounts for 30 ± 36%. Predation on commercial cockles (minimum length of 30mm) is less than 200 tonnes in years of low production and reaches 400 tonnes in good years. © 2024 Societe d'Etudes Ornithologiques. All rights reserved.},
