	abstract = {Abstract: Regression analysis of the size and weight structure of dreissenids (D. bugensis and D. polymorpha) from the Volgograd Reservoir has been carried out. The power-dependence parameters in the resulting equation are different for the two studied mollusk species (W = 0.036L<sup>3.33</sup> for D. bugensis and W = 0.064L<sup>3.32</sup>) for D. polymorpha. The established regression relationship between the individual body weight (W) and the shell length of the mollusk (L) has a high degree of correlation R<sup>2</sup> = 0.96 at a significance level of p = 0.01. The results can be used for reconstructing the individual weight of mollusks from the shell length during trophological studies in Lower Volga reservoirs. © 2018, Pleiades Publishing, Inc.},
