	affiliations = {El Colegio de la Frontera Sur, Admin. de Correos No. 2, Atasta, C.P. 86168, Villahermosa, Tabasco, Apartado Postal 1042, Mexico; Department of Soil Science, 53115 Bonn, Nussallee 13, Germany; Forstamt Kottenforst, 53123 Bonn, Flerzheimer Allee 121, Germany},
	abstract = {We investigated the initial effects of strip wise soil loosening (0-35 cm depth) on soil chemical and physical parameters by using a deeply working rotary cultivator in combination with liming and mixing of the dolomite with the soil material of acidic forests. The investigations took place 8 months after the treatment. pH values and contents of exchangeable Ca and Mg increased significantly at the tilled depth whereas the content of exchangeable Al and easily soluble P decreased. The rate of mineralisation increased at this depth which was shown by a loss of Corg, Ntot and short-term loss of NO<sub>3</sub>-N. The treatment led to a mobilisation of Mn at the tilled depth. However, the content of exchangeable Pb decreased due to an increased pH value. Below the tillage depth of 35 cm only partly significant changes of exchangeable Mn and NO<sub>3</sub>-N were found. The total porosity and bulk density at 10-15 and 40-45 cm depths were not significantly different from those in the control plot, but the rate of infiltration increased significantly. © 2002 Elsevier Science B.V. All rights reserved.},
